    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nI tried to comment out parts of a line, but it only ever comments out the whole line.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.0-dev-74+gae9654dd73\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua foo.js`\r\n2. Have the cursor on `bar`, hit `gci(` (or make a visual selection of anything and hit `gc`)\r\n\r\nminimal.lua:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal lazydatapath = \"/tmp/minimal/lazy\"\r\nlocal lazypath = lazydatapath .. \"/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n  vim.fn.system({\r\n    \"git\",\r\n    \"clone\",\r\n    \"--filter=blob:none\",\r\n    \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\",\r\n    \"--branch=stable\", -- latest stable release\r\n    lazypath,\r\n  })\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup({\r\n  root = lazydatapath,\r\n  spec = {\r\n    \"echasnovski/mini.comment\",\r\n    config = function()\r\n      require(\"mini.comment\").setup()\r\n    end,\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nfoo.js:\r\n```js\r\nconst foo = (bar) => {\r\n}\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n```js\r\nconst foo = (/* bar */) => {\r\n}\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n```js\r\n// const foo = (bar) => {\r\n}\r\n```",
