        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is in README in title: \"Comment lines\". And no need to look at source code, as this information is also in [the top of help file](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4716f26d7288e5f6de902480b3f3d045e3dd3f42/doc/mini-comment.txt#L17-L18) and there is a link to help file in the top of README. I'll think about adding more explicit wording in README.\r\n\r\nThe main reason this is out of scope is because there is no reliable built-in way to get information about how language is expected to do inline comment. For per-line commenting there is 'commentstring' option (which is mentioned in README), but for inline comments one should have to manually keep this information inside module. As dealing with language specific configurations is out of scope for 'mini.nvim' in general, this is also out of scope for 'mini.comment'.\r\n\r\nClosing as it will change.",
